meta {
  name: 05 Start checkout
  type: http
  seq: 5
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/payments/{{paymentId}}/checkout
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "provider": "fapshi"
  }
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.body.paymentId: eq {{paymentId}}
  res.body.provider: isDefined
  res.body.checkoutUrl: isDefined
}

docs {
  Where the center goes to pay for a PENDING payment. Run
  `02 Create payment` first — it captures `{{paymentId}}`.

  Body (required):
  - `"provider": "fapshi"` — Mobile Money (Orange / MTN via Fapshi)
  - `"provider": "stripe"` — card

  Both methods can be configured on the server at once; the body picks which.
  Local smoke with fake provider: use `06 Simulate provider webhook` after
  checkout (or skip checkout and webhook a PENDING payment created under
  PAYMENT_PROVIDER=fake).

  ## The server must have that method configured

  Missing keys for the chosen method → 503 PAYMENT_PROVIDER_NOT_CONFIGURED.

  For local testing with the fake (tests / Bruno simulate webhook):

      PAYMENT_PROVIDER=fake
      FAKE_PAYMENT_WEBHOOK_SECRET=<any value of 32 characters or more>

  Never set PAYMENT_PROVIDER=fake on DigitalOcean.

  For real methods, set Notch and/or Stripe keys (see `.env.example`). They
  register independently — fill both to offer MM and card.

  ## What to check by hand

  1. SEND IT TWICE. Both return the SAME `checkoutUrl`.
  2. THE PROVIDER REFERENCE IS NOT IN THE RESPONSE.
  3. A PAID OR FAILED PAYMENT -> 409 PAYMENT_NOT_PENDING.
  4. ANOTHER CENTER'S PAYMENT -> 404, never 403.

  ## While BLOCKED

  This works. Paying is how a lapsed center comes back.
}
